Download paid apps the account owns from Google Play.

Play answers /purchase for a paid app with HTTP 400 whether or not the
account owns it, so gpapi got no delivery token and gave up with
InvalidApp. Ask /delivery without a token in that case, as Aurora Store
does: it serves an owned app and reports status 3 for one that hasn't
been bought. Say why when Play refuses a delivery.

Upstream treats paid apps as unsupported:
https://github.com/EFForg/apkeep/issues/190

